<article>


<h2>Incoming Students</h2>

<h3>Students</h3>


<a name="exchange"></a>
<h4>Exchange students</h4>
<p><strong>WHO:</strong> Undergraduate and graduate students enrolled in institutions that have an exchange agreement with PUC-Rio. In addition to the Portuguese as a Second Language (required) course, these students may attend other regular courses according to her/his area of interest.</p>
<p><strong>CREDITS:</strong> Academic credits are obtained.</p>
<p><strong>TRANSCRIPT:</strong> The student will receive an official PUC-Rio transcript listing the courses taken with its corresponding total number of class-hours, number of credits obtained and the final course grade.</p>
<p><strong>APPLICATION:</strong> In addition to the specific exchange program requirements and application process of the student&acute;s home institution and study abroad office, the student must also observe all the requirements and deadlines of the PUC-Rio application process.</p>
<p><strong>Required documents:</strong> Online application forms filled out, upload the required documents. Personal Statement (introduce yourself and why you would like to study at PUC-Rio), Official Transcript, Copy of health insurance with company name and policy number covering COVID 19 <strong><u>(recommended)</u></strong>, a copy of passport (main  page), 01 photo (3 cm x 4cm),<strong> Covid 19 Certificate of vaccination, <u>Yellow fever immunization (recommended),</u></strong> the administrative cost  payment.</p>
<p>Please visit the following website to fill out the  online application, and see the required documents to send  and for more information: <a href="forms-hp_students.html">http://www.puc-rio.br/ensinopesq/ccci/incoming/forms-hp_students.html</a></p>
<p><strong>a) Students must send the  required documents to PUC-Rio:</strong></p>
<p>Please visit the following site to fill out the  online application form: <a href="forms-hp_students.html">http://www.puc-rio.br/ensinopesq/ccci/incoming/forms-hp_students.html</a></p>
<p class="puc_texto_destaque">DEADLINES</p>
<ul>
  <strong>April</strong><strong>15th</strong> (exchange period starting in Jul-Aug)
  <li><strong>October 15th</strong> (exchange period starting in Feb/Mar)</li>
</ul>
<p><strong>TUITION / FEES:</strong> Exchange students do not pay tuition.</p>
<p><strong>An administrative cost</strong> is charged. International students are allowed to attend courses at PUC-Rio up to two regular terms plus the Pre-Term Portuguese as a second language Intensive Course.</p>
<p> Students registered for a year or those  who request extension of the student exchange period, will pay the renewal of the <strong> administrative cost</strong> charged 
  
  during the deadline for the Exchange Period Extension.</p>
<p>For current costs of tuition and fees, please  refer to: <a href="fees_tuition.html">http://www.puc-rio.br/ensinopesq/ccci/incoming/fees_tuition.html</a></p>
<p><strong>VISA:</strong> A student visa is required. The visa must be obtained <strong>BEFORE</strong> the student&acute;s  entrance in Brazil. A tourist visa cannot be transferred  into a student visa  inside the country. When the applicant is accepted, CCCI will send a  LETTER OF ACCEPTANCE that will enable him/her to obtain a visa at a Brazilian  Consulate.</p>
<!-- Botão voltar -->
<button onclick="javascript:history.back()" class="puc_link_voltar_TAG-BUTTON" title="Back">BACK</button>

<hr>
<a name="independent"></a>

<h4>Independent students</h4>
<p><strong>WHO:</strong> Undergraduate  and graduate students enrolled in institutions that do not have an exchange  agreement with PUC-Rio. In addition to the Portuguese as  a second language (required) course, these students  may attend other regular courses according to his/her area of interest. </p>
<p><strong>CREDITS:</strong> Academic credits are obtained.</p>
<p><strong>TRANSCRIPT:</strong> The student will receive an official PUC-Rio transcript listing the  courses taken with its  corresponding total number of class-hours, number of credits obtained  and the final course grade.</p>
<p><strong>APPLICATION:</strong> The procedures for Independent   Student registration are the following:</p>
<p><strong>a) Required documents:</strong> Online application forms filled out, upload the required documents. Personal Statement (introduce  yourself and why you would like to study at PUC-Rio), <strong>02  recommendation letters (originals and signed), </strong>Official Transcript, Copy  of health insurance with company name and policy number covering COVID 19,  <strong><u>(recommended)</u></strong> a copy of passport (main page), 01 photo (3 cm  x 4cm),<strong> Covid 19 Certificate of vaccination, <u> </u><u>Yellow fever immunization (recommended),</u></strong> the administrative cost  payment.</p>
<p>Please visit the following website to  fill out the online application<strong>, see the  required documents to send&nbsp; and for more  information: <a href="forms-hp_students.html">http://www.puc-rio.br/ensinopesq/ccci/incoming/forms-hp_students.html</a></strong></p>
<p class="puc_texto_destaque">DEADLINES for submitting applications:</p>
<ul><li><strong>April</strong><strong> 15th</strong> (exchange period starting in Jul-Aug)</li>
  <li><strong>October 15th</strong> (exchange period starting in 
    
    Feb/Mar)</li>
</ul>
<p><strong>b)</strong> Upon acceptance of the  applicant, CCCI will send him/her a LETTER OF ACCEPTANCE  that will enable him/her to obtain a student visa  at a Brazilian Consulate. </p>
<p><strong>c) TO REGISTER:</strong> The student must present  him/herself at The International Office - CCCI one week before the first day of classes to confirm  registration with a copy of the letter of acceptance sent by CCCI and the passport  with a STUDENT VISA valid for the entire academic period. Students will not be registered  without the appropriate visa. </p>
<p><strong>TUITION/FEES: An  administrative cost is charged</strong>. Independent   Students pay tuition.</p>
<p>The academic tuition will be charged according to the number of credits taken in each term. In Brazil, the yearly tuition is divided into 12 monthly payments. The semester (term) tuition is divided into 6 monthly installments for regular students. Thus, in our first term of the year (late February/early March to late June/early July), students make 6 payments: in January, February, March, April, May and June; The same happens in the second term, with payments in July, August, September, October, November and December.</p>
<p><strong>For the international students it is divided differently, based on the date of arrival.</strong></p>
<p>Because  international exchange and Independent  students arrive at the university only in the second month  of the semester, the semester tuition will be divided into 4 installments  (March, April, May, June), THE FIRST TWO INSTALLMENTS  EQUAL the sum of 2 monthly  tuition payments each. In  case of a late  registration, the total tuition  amount will be divided  into 3 monthly payments (April, May, June).</p>
<p>Please refer to <a href="fees_tuition.html">http://www.puc-rio.br/ensinopesq/ccci/incoming/fees_tuition.html</a> to get more information  about the tuitions and fees.</p>
<p class="puc_texto_destaque">Method of Payment:<br>
  The fees must be paid in Reais (R$), according to the dollar rate of the day.</p>
<p><strong>Independent Students  will receive by e-mail the bill and the payment must be done before the 3<sup>rd</sup> day of the month, in order to avoid an extra fine.</strong></p>
<p><strong>REMEMBER  THAT, ACCORDING TO THE NEW DELIBERATION FOR INTERNATIONAL STUDENTS, YOU ARE  ALLOWED TO ATTEND A MAXIMUM OF 5 COURSES, CORRESPONDING TO A MAXIMUM OF 24  CREDITS, AND A MINIMUM OF 2 COURSES OR 08 CREDITS PER SEMESTER AT PUC-RIO</strong>.  (Remember that the exchange rate fluctuates in Brazil).</p>
<p><strong>An administrative cost</strong>&nbsp;is charged. International students are allowed to attend courses  at PUC-Rio up to two regular terms plus the Pre-Term Portuguese as a second  language Intensive Course. </p>
<p>Independent   Students are entitled to attend courses at PUC-Rio for up to two regular terms plus the  Intensive Pre-Term Portuguese Course.</p>
<p>Students  registered for a year or those who request extension of the student exchange  period, must pay  the renewal of the <strong> administrative cost </strong> charged during the deadline for  the Exchange Period Extension. For more information about tuition and fees,  please refer to: <a href="fees_tuition.html">http://www.puc-rio.br/ensinopesq/ccci/incoming/fees_tuition.html</a></p>
<p><strong>VISA:</strong> Student  visa is required. The visa must be obtained BEFORE the entrance in Brazil. A  tourist visa cannot  be transferred into a student visa once inside the country.</p>
<p><span class="puc_texto_destaque">IMPORTANT:</span> for next year the tuition and fees are going to  change. Please see the Tuition and fees link: <a href="fees_tuition.html">http://www.puc-rio.br/ensinopesq/ccci/incoming/fees_tuition.html</a></p>


<h4><br>
  Independent  Student - Portuguese as Second Language Regular Semester/Year</h4>
<p><strong>WHO:</strong> Undergraduate and graduate students, professionals  or any adult  (minimum age: 18) with a full secondary school degree. In addition to Portuguese  as a Second Language course (required), the student may attend other regular  courses according to his/her area of interest.</p>
<p>The Portuguese as a Second  Language regular semester &nbsp;course is  designed to develop the students&rsquo; ability to understand and use both spoken and  written Portuguese, in order to develop communication skills.</p>
<p><strong>CREDITS:</strong> Academic credits are only obtained upon completion of regular semester courses.</p>
<p><strong>TRANSCRIPT:</strong> The student will receive  an official PUC-Rio transcript listing the courses taken with its corresponding  total number of class hours, the number of credits obtained and the final course  grade. </p>
<p><strong>APPLICATION:</strong> The procedures for Independent   Student registration are the following:</p>
<p><strong>a) Required  documents:</strong>&nbsp;Online application forms filled out, Personal  Statement (introduce yourself and why you would like to study at  PUC-Rio),&nbsp;<strong>02  recommendation letters (originals and signed),&nbsp;</strong>Official  Transcript, Copy of health insurance with company name and policy number covering COVID 19,  a copy of passport (main page), 01 photo (3 cm  x 4cm),<strong> Covid 19 Certificate of  vaccination, <u> Yellow fever immunization ( recommended),</u></strong> the administrative cost payment.</p>
<p>Please visit the following website to  download the application<strong>, see the  required documents to send,&nbsp; and for more  information: <a href="forms-hp_students.html">http://www.puc-rio.br/ensinopesq/ccci/incoming/forms-hp_students.html</a></strong></p>
<p class="puc_texto_destaque"> DEADLINES for submitting  applications:</p>
<ul>
  <li><strong>April 15th</strong> (exchange period starting in Jul-Aug)</li>
  <li><strong>October 15th</strong> (exchange period  starting in Feb/Mar) </li>
</ul>
<p><strong>b)</strong> Upon acceptance of the  applicant, CCCI will send him/her a LETTER OF ACCEPTANCE that will enable him/her to obtain a student visa  at a Brazilian Consulate.</p>
<p><strong>c) TO REGISTER:</strong> The  student must present him/herself at The International Office - CCCI one week before the first day of  classes to confirm registration with a copy of the letter of acceptance sent by  CCCI and the passport with a STUDENT VISA valid for the entire academic period.  Students will not be registered without the appropriate visa. </p>
<p><strong>TUITION/FEES:</strong> The academic tuition will be charged  according to the number of credits taken in each term. In Brazil, the yearly  tuition is divided into 12 monthly payments. The semester (term) tuition is  divided into 6 monthly installments for regular students. Thus, in our first  term of the year (late February/early March to late June/early July), students  make 6 payments: in January, February, March, April, May and June; The same  happens in the second term, with payments in July, August, September, October,  November and December. </p>
<p><strong>For the international students it is divided differently,  based on the date of arrival.</strong></p>
<p>Because international  exchange and Independent  students arrive to the university only in the second month  of the semester, the semester tuition will be divided into 4 installments  (March, April, May, June), THE FIRST TWO INSTALLMENTS ARE EQUAL to the sum of 2  monthly tuition payments each. In  case of a late registration, the total tuition  amount will be divided into 3 monthly payments (April, May, June). International non-degree-seeking students are part of the Center of Theology  and Human Sciences (CTCH) due to their attendance of the mandatory Portuguese  classes. </p>
<p>Please refer to <a href="fees_tuition.html">http://www.puc-rio.br/ensinopesq/ccci/incoming/fees_tuition.html</a> to get more  information about the tuitions and fees. </p>
<p><strong>Method of Payment:</strong></p>
<p>The  fees must be paid in Reais (R$), according to the dollar rate of the day.</p>
<p><strong>REMEMBER THAT, ACCORDING TO THE NEW  DELIBERATION FOR INTERNATIONAL STUDENTS, YOU ARE ALLOWED TO ATTEND A MAXIMUM OF  5 COURSES, CORRESPONDING TO A MAXIMUM OF 24 CREDITS, AND A MINIMUM OF 2 COURSES  OR 08 CREDITS PER SEMESTER AT PUC-RIO</strong>. (Remember that the exchange rate fluctuates  in Brazil). </p>
<p><strong>An administrative cost</strong>&nbsp;is charged. International Students are allowed to attend courses  at PUC-Rio up to two regular terms plus the Pre-Term Portuguese as a second  language Intensive Course. </p>
<p>Independent  Students are entitled to attend  courses at PUC-Rio for up to two regular terms plus the Intensive Pre-Term  Portuguese Course. </p>
<p>Students registered for a year or those who  request extension of the student exchange period, must pay the renewal of the <strong>administrative cost </strong> charged during the deadline for the Exchange Period  Extension. </p>
<p><strong>VISA:</strong> Student visa is required.  The visa must be obtained BEFORE the entrance in Brazil. A tourist visa cannot  be transferred into a student visa once inside the country.</p>
<!-- Botão voltar -->
<button onclick="javascript:history.back()" class="puc_link_voltar_TAG-BUTTON" title="Back">BACK</button>

<hr>
<a name="double"></a>

<h4>Double Degree Students</h4>
<p><strong>WHO: </strong>Double  Degree is a program between PUC-Rio and:</p>

<ul class="puc_lista_especial_TAG-UL">
<li>America</li>
</ul>



<table width="81%" align="center" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" class="puc_tabela_padrao_TAG-TABLE">
<tr class="puc_tabela_linha_n1_TAG-TR">
<td colspan="3">Peru</td>
</tr>
<tr class="puc_tabela_linha_escura_TAG-TR">
